# Majorana modes and the Ising fusion ring. A Majorana operator is its own antiparticle, and braiding the unpaired
# Majorana modes at the ends of a Kitaev chain realizes the Ising anyons, the three objects of the Ising theory: the
# vacuum, the Majorana fermion psi, and the sigma anyon that a Majorana zero mode carries. Their fusion is the Ising rule:
# the fermion is its own inverse, psi times psi is the vacuum, fusing psi with sigma gives sigma back, and two sigmas fuse
# to either the vacuum or the fermion, sigma times sigma is one plus psi. This file DEFINES those fusion multiplicities as
# a function on the three labels and PROVES the ring laws: the vacuum is a unit, fusion is commutative, and the Majorana
# fermion squares to the vacuum, which is exactly the statement that a Majorana is its own antiparticle. Every theorem is
# quantified over the actual three-element anyon type and checked by induction.

# The three Ising anyons: the vacuum, the Majorana fermion psi, and the sigma anyon of a Majorana zero mode.
form ising
  case vacuum
  case psi
  case sigma

# The Kronecker delta on Ising anyons, one when the labels agree.
task same-ising
  take b, like ising
  take c, like ising
  like natural-number
  fork case, read b
    case vacuum
      fork case, read c
        case vacuum
          send back
            code 1
        case psi
          send back
            code 0
        case sigma
          send back
            code 0
    case psi
      fork case, read c
        case vacuum
          send back
            code 0
        case psi
          send back
            code 1
        case sigma
          send back
            code 0
    case sigma
      fork case, read c
        case vacuum
          send back
            code 0
        case psi
          send back
            code 0
        case sigma
          send back
            code 1

# One when c is not sigma, the multiplicity of c in sigma times sigma, which is the vacuum plus psi.
task not-sigma
  take c, like ising
  like natural-number
  fork case, read c
    case vacuum
      send back
        code 1
    case psi
      send back
        code 1
    case sigma
      send back
        code 0

# The Ising fusion multiplicity: how many times c appears in a times b, the structure constants of the Ising ring.
task combine
  take a, like ising
  take b, like ising
  take c, like ising
  like natural-number
  fork case, read a
    case vacuum
      send back
        call same-ising
          read b
          read c
    case psi
      fork case, read b
        case vacuum
          send back
            call same-ising
              make psi
              read c
        case psi
          send back
            call same-ising
              make vacuum
              read c
        case sigma
          send back
            call same-ising
              make sigma
              read c
    case sigma
      fork case, read b
        case vacuum
          send back
            call same-ising
              make sigma
              read c
        case psi
          send back
            call same-ising
              make sigma
              read c
        case sigma
          send back
            call not-sigma
              read c

# THE VACUUM IS A UNIT: fusing the vacuum with any anyon b returns exactly b, combine(vacuum, b, c) = same-ising(b, c),
# for all b and c. Proved by induction over the anyon labels.
rule vacuum-is-the-fusion-unit
  seat b, like ising
  seat c, like ising
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call combine
        make vacuum
        read b
        read c
      call same-ising
        read b
        read c
  fold b, c

# FUSION IS COMMUTATIVE: the multiplicity is unchanged when the two factors are swapped, combine(a, b, c) = combine(b, a,
# c), for all a, b and c. Proved by simultaneous induction over the three anyon labels, the full twenty-seven-case grid.
rule fusion-is-commutative
  seat a, like ising
  seat b, like ising
  seat c, like ising
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call combine
        read a
        read b
        read c
      call combine
        read b
        read a
        read c
  fold a, b, c

# THE MAJORANA IS ITS OWN ANTIPARTICLE: the fermion psi fused with itself gives the vacuum, combine(psi, psi, c) =
# same-ising(vacuum, c), for all c, so psi times psi is one. This is the defining property of a Majorana, that it is its
# own antiparticle. Proved by induction over the third label.
rule the-majorana-is-its-own-antiparticle
  seat c, like ising
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call combine
        make psi
        make psi
        read c
      call same-ising
        make vacuum
        read c
  fold c
